## 2. Security Governance Model

1. **Pre-Flight AST Inspection:** Before any agent-synthesized code reaches compute infrastructure, `ASTGovernancePolicy` inspects syntax trees for forbidden module imports, direct builtin calls (`eval`, `exec`), and attribute tampering (`__subclasses__`, `__builtins__`).
2. **Cryptographic Capability Tokens:** Validated code hashes are bound to short-lived (30s) HMAC-SHA256 signature tokens. The Cloud Run sandbox rejects requests lacking a valid, unexpired token matching the exact payload hash.
3. **Isolated Execution Environment:** Code runs inside ephemeral Cloud Run micro-VMs (gVisor gen2) with a read-only root filesystem, strict memory caps (512 MiB), and execution timeouts (15s).

